the Plane of Fire. If I have not sufficient scrolls and nothing to write
them I can successfully use other methods. On Eart I blindfold myself and
see in which reagions the monsters disappear, or the other way round, if
you know where the caverns are you can identify the cavern with the portal
as the one where there are no monsters or not as many monsters as you'd
expect the size of the cavern should have. On the Plane of Air I used a
wand of secret door detection, zapped in a raw grid on the right side of
the map so that a single wand will suffice. On the Plane of Water - I do
not levitate though the water - you can wear the Amulet of Yendor to get
hints where to look for the portal and additionally you may zap remaining
charges from secret door detection when the bubble covers a large area.
I seem to recall to have used the Bell of Opening's remaining charges as
a substitute for a wand of secret door detection. You can combine some of
